$ yo test --help
Usage: yo test [path] [options]

Run *.test.yo files (a file, a directory tree, or the whole workspace).

Options:
  -b, --bail                Stop after the first failure
  -v, --verbose             Show detailed output and errors
  --test-name-pattern <re>  Run only tests whose name matches the regex <re>
  --exclude <path>          Exclude a directory/file (repeatable)
  --workspace               Run every workspace member's tests in one run
  --shard <i>/<n>           Run only every n-th collected file, offset i
  --list                    List the tests that would run (file<TAB>name);
                            nothing is compiled
  --json                    One JSON object per line: a "test" event per test
                            (file, name, status, duration_ms; message and
                            output on failure) and a closing "summary" event;
                            human output is suppressed
  --json-summary            Append the {"passed","failed","total"} line to the
                            human summary
  -p, --parallel <n>        Accepted for compatibility (v1 runs sequentially)
  --test-batch-size <n>     Tests per generated C batch (default 100)
  --cc, --c-compiler <cc>   C compiler for test binaries
  --target <triple>         Run tests for a cross target (e.g. wasm32-wasip1)
  --allocator <name>        Allocator for test binaries (system|mimalloc|fixed)
  --heap-size <size>        Fixed-region heap, e.g. 16M (only with --allocator fixed)
  --debug-heap              Heap stats + live-at-exit oracle per test (fixed only)
  --disable-sanitize        Skip AddressSanitizer linkage
  -k, --keep-generated-files  Keep generated batch files
  --profile                 Print per-phase timing
  --std-path <dir>          Override the std library directory

Environment:
  YO_KEEP_BATCH=1           Leave the generated batch .yo/.c files in place
  YO_TEST_SANITIZE=<kind>   Sanitizer for test binaries (default address)
  YO_TEST_LEAK_VERDICT=0    Do not fail a test on a LeakSanitizer report

Examples:
  $ yo test                       All tests in the workspace
  $ yo test ./tests --bail
  $ yo test ./tests/fs/temp.test.yo --test-name-pattern "Dispose"
  $ yo test ./tests --list
  $ yo test ./tests/fs --json
